QUESTION: is the d>=3.5 MAIN-band qf-seed lift (fires on ALL is_screenshot at
d>=3.5) pure downside on HIGH-colour (m3 in [24,80)) screenshots? Task #12 fixed
the LOW-colour photo leak; the residual was framed as "high-colour main-band
misfire (windows95/9291)". Hypothesis (task #13): exclude high-colour from the
main band.

METHOD — the byte-ratio proxy (cjxl_bytes / our_lift_off_bytes at MATCHED
DISTANCE) used earlier is WRONG for evaluating the lift: it compares cjxl and
lift_off at the d4 target and never scores the lift_on point. The correct metric
is RD-EFFICIENCY at MATCHED QUALITY: encode our lift_on (default e7 d4) -> ssim2_on;
build cjxl's RD curve (d 0.5..4.0); interpolate the cjxl bytes needed to reach
ssim2_on; efficiency = cjxl_bytes_at_ssim2_on / lift_on_bytes. >1.25 = lift reaches
that quality MORE efficiently than cjxl (genuine WIN); ~1 = lift sits ON cjxl's own
curve (neutral — it only overshoots the requested distance, no RD advantage); <0.95
= lift RD-dominated (LOSS).

RESULT — colour does NOT separate wins from non-wins (HYPOTHESIS REFUTED):
  LOW-ship  (n=4): imac_dark 2.22x WIN, imac_g3 2.62x WIN, graph 0.89x LOSS, gmessages 0.94x LOSS
  HIGH      (n=8): w8221 2.32x WIN, w8102 1.55x WIN, w8330 1.30x WIN,
                   w8160 1.19x, imessage 1.03x, windows95 0.98x, ing9291 0.95x, w8274 0.85x LOSS
  HIGH-colour contains GENUINE RD WINS (w8221 2.32x reaches ssim2 87 at 137KB vs
  cjxl 317KB). A blanket high-colour exclude would DESTROY them. The earlier
  byte-ratio "misfire" (windows95 0.98x cjxl/lift_off) was the lift overshooting
  the requested d4 target to a point ON cjxl's curve (ssim2 86 at 43KB == cjxl
  43KB) — deliberate screenshot-quality design, NOT RD waste.

CANDIDATE DISCRIMINATOR (lead for the proper re-baseline sweep, NOT shipped):
  luma_var / detail level, NOT colour. The 3 LOSSES cluster at luma_var <= 1223
  (graph 415, gmessages 1046, w8274 1223); every WIN has luma_var >= 3162
  (imac_dark 3303, imac_g3 5244, w8102 3162, w8221 3264, w8330 5522). edge_density
  agrees (losses ed<=0.07, wins ed 0.11-0.16). Interpretation: on flat low-detail
  UI the lift overshoots into near-lossless where cjxl is already efficient; on
  detailed content the fine-quant lift pays off. NOTE the LOSS verdicts are the
  WEAKEST (0.85-0.94x, near break-even, ssim2_on 89-90 where cjxl's high-q curve
  is steep and interpolation is noisiest); the WIN verdicts (1.3-2.6x) are robust.

VERDICT: task #13 (exclude high-colour) is REFUTED — do not ship. The main-band
lift is broadly RD-positive-or-neutral; it is not colour-separable. A luma_var
(detail) gate is a candidate but needs the proper dense, Pareto-scored (bytes AND
ssim2), SHIP-validated screenshot-gate re-baseline sweep on imazen-26 8000/8100 +
gb82-sc (the standing CLAUDE.md "re-baseline screenshot-class gates" follow-on),
NOT a 12-cell inline flip. n=12 is a lead, not a calibration.

CAVEAT: single-encode, one distance (d4), 12 cells. score_jxl_files interpolation
at the high-q end (ssim2>=89) is noisy. The WIN signal (high-colour cells reaching
matched quality at 1.3-2.6x fewer bytes than cjxl) is the robust, decision-relevant
finding; the near-break-even LOSSES are not.
